# SRG-APP-000026-AU-000580  -  CAT II
# The Central Log Server must automatically audit account creation.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000026-AU-000580
group:           V-221900
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000018
control_rev5:    AC-2

contribution:    Splunk writes an audit event for administrative actions on accounts,
                 account creation included, without a switch to turn that generation on or
                 off; the one application setting bearing on the requirement is whether
                 those audit events are placed on the index queue so the record is retained
                 and searchable rather than only written to the audit log file.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.

check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing not_equals false

external:        Accounts created in an external identity store - LDAP, SAML, or a scripted
                 authentication provider - are created outside Splunk, so the creation
                 record for those identities is generated by the directory service or
                 identity provider and forwarded to Splunk as data; Splunk audits only the
                 account actions performed on itself.
external:        Where audit queueing is set to false by design, an inputs.conf monitor
                 stanza tailing the audit log carries the retention of these records.
external:        The retention period applied to the audit index, and review of the
                 resulting records, are organizational determinations.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/audit.conf.spec:23-29 ([auditTrail] queueing =
                 <boolean>, default true); audit.conf declares no other setting in 10.x,
                 and the _audit destination named in the check inventory is not a
                 configurable key in the specification; SRG-APP-000026-AU-000580 check and
                 fix text.
finding:         Audit records for account creation are generated by Splunk but not
                 retained in an index, because audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing is set to
                 false and no compensating monitor input is configured; this is assessed at
                 the application layer alone, and accounts created in an external directory
                 service or identity provider are audited by that component, which is
                 recorded as an external dependency.
